  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="666d3cc7-fa12-58e8-9e8f-41fb93d833b8" activityNameId="26e6c9cd-e73d-552b-8e19-f48d80aae5b0" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Nuclear power plant, pressure water reactor 1000MW
Estimation based on data of the power plant in Gösgen with a net installed capacity of 970 MW (constant capacity over 1996 - 2002). Material and energy data were extrapolated from the information available for the BWR in Leibstadt and used for the module "nuclear power plant, boiling water reactor", CH. Waste material inventory data for decommissioning of the power plant in Gösgen were available from the evaluation performed by the operators during the 1980s.;
UUID: cba5bf71-5887-3432-8975-795b6dd15a21
The module includes materials, energy and transport requirements used for construction of the plant. Land-use is included with the assumption of 40 years operation. Disposal of non-contaminated material from dismantling is also included, whereas contaminated materials are attributed to the operation.
Location: Swiss data of one specific plant.
Technology: The described plant Gösgen started commercial operation at the end of 1979. It belongs to the 1000 MW class. It has a Siemens designed primary circuit with three loop cooling, a spherical containment, and a cooling tower. This module can be assumed to be representative for other pressure water reactors of the same class in Western Europe.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cba5bf71-5887-3432-8975-795b6dd15a21.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
